<title>HONG KONG: NatWest ups warrants on Hong Kong property basket.</title>
<headline>NatWest ups warrants on Hong Kong property basket.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>NatWest Financial Products Plc said on Friday it had issued a further 179 million American-style call warrants on a basket of four blue-chip property stocks, on top of an earlier issue of 239 million warrants.</p>
<p>Each basket comprises:</p>
<p> Cheung Kong (Holdings) Ltd	     0.05  shares</p>
<p> Sun Hung Kai Properties Ltd	    0.04  shares</p>
<p> New World Development Co Ltd	   0.075 shares</p>
<p> Henderson Land Development Co Ltd    0.02  shares</p>
<p>Ten warrants control one basket.</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE	HK$11.7225   PREMIUM	 11.8 PCT</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE	 HK$0.278     GEARING	 4.7x</p>
<p> LAUNCH DATE	 30.MAY.97    LISTING DATE  06.JUN.97</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	  20.MAY.98    PAYDATE	 05.JUN.97</p>
<p> LISTING	     HONG KONG    MIN EXER LOT  10,000</p>
<p> SPOT REFERENCE    HK$12.973</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
